// bubbler profile: steam
//
// The client is a 32-bit i386 binary and its UI (steamwebhelper) is an
// X11/CEF client with no Wayland support, so this profile needs both
// `seccomp { disable }` — the filter holds one architecture and kills an
// i386 process rather than filtering it — and `x11`. The Arch wiki's own
// bwrap example carries an accuracy dispute over exactly that forwarding:
// an X11 client can keylog and inject into every other X11 client,
// Xwayland included.
//
// Never add `userns "disable"`: Proton and the Steam Linux Runtime nest
// their own bubblewrap (pressure-vessel ships srt-bwrap), which has to
// create a user namespace inside this one.
//
// No `portals`: that grant writes /.flatpak-info, and Steam's runtime
// reads it as "I am the unofficial Steam Flatpak" —
// steam-runtime-check-requirements then demands the flatpak-portal
// service and exits 71, so steam.sh stops before the client starts
// (measured). Steam brings its own file browser; a path outside the
// private home is shared below instead.
//
// Steam builds its own ~/.steam and ~/.local/share/Steam in the private
// home on first run. The host's are not shared, because ~/.steam is a
// directory of absolute symlinks into the host home; move an existing
// install in instead, with the instance stopped:
//   mv ~/.local/share/Steam ~/.local/share/bubbler/instances/steam/home/.local/share/
// A library folder on another disk is named explicitly, e.g.
//   path-share "/kioxia/Steam" mode=rw
// Steam Input's virtual controllers need two more grants, each with a
// warning of its own in the README:
//   gamepad hidraw=#true uinput=#true
// The host side is multilib 32-bit GL and Vulkan drivers and an
// en_US.UTF-8 locale; the locale reaches the sandbox through LANG and the
// read-only /usr, with nothing to bind for it.
wayland
x11
dri
pipewire
network
dbus {
    own "com.steampowered.*"
    talk "org.freedesktop.ScreenSaver"
    talk "org.freedesktop.PowerManagement"
}
notify
tray
gamepad
system-bus {
    talk "org.freedesktop.UPower"
    talk "org.freedesktop.UDisks2"
}
seccomp {
    disable
}
command "steam"
